    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is our clear headliner with a 76.13 efficiency score. Despite the daunting matchup against Grayson Rodriguez, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** maintains elite status due to the favorable batting order (#3) and a strong park factor that elevates his floor against a high-ERA arm. **Jonathan Aranda** also surfaces as an essential start (67.64) thanks to a rare combination of an excellent batting spot (#2) and a significant +12% platoon edge against Melton. While **Zack Gelof** (60.79) faces a tougher lefty in Connor Prielipp, his aggressive placement at #3 and the park factors outweigh the minor SB-suppression risk, making him a solid anchor for our middle infield.\n\nThe bench decision process was tight, with **Luis Arraez** (49.17) narrowly missing the cut. While **Luis Arraez** offers a reliable profile, the optimizer favored the higher platoon-adjusted upside provided by **Gavin Sheets** and the overall efficiency of our starting corner infielders. We continue to monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for the entire squad; specifically, the output for **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, and **Dylan Beavers** could shift significantly once official cards are posted. **Bryce Harper** (55.27) remains a high-variance play against Bryan Woo\u2014though his xwOBA of 0.392 provides a layer of security, the SP skill of Woo combined with park headwinds makes him a borderline start that we are keeping in the lineup purely for his ceiling.\n\nRisks remain prevalent, particularly with the lefty-heavy matchups for **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Cal Raleigh**, all of whom are facing difficult southpaws. **Jung Hoo Lee** (56.48) is battling a significant -10% platoon penalty, though his score is buoyed by his historical ability to steal bases against slower-delivering pitchers. We are keeping **Gleyber Torres** (52.13) in the lineup, but proceed with caution as his -13% platoon impact against Freddy Peralta is the largest negative situational factor on our board. We remain diligent about these matchups to protect our categorical efficiency as we push toward the season end.",
